  "testsPassed": 27,
  "tests": [
    "installation preserves existing Auth, profiles, sessions, objects and bucket privacy",
    "cutover aborts before touching an existing business session or replacing a custom request hook",
    "seven internal tables and every helper are private; only four provider contracts allow service execution",
    "personal, staff and anonymous sessions retain the existing request and RLS behavior",
    "a business token without an actual bound session fails request hook and direct RLS",
    "owner bootstrap is explicit, current personal ownership is required and one seat is created",
    "owner launch rejects substituted, deleted, expired, deactivated and banned personal sessions",
    "previously banned or deactivated businesses remain unavailable and are never enabled",
    "ordinary member devices are pending and need explicit approval before a grant exists",
    "first owner consent does not auto-approve subsequent or previously pending devices",
    "device ID knowledge and forged proof cannot take over an approved or pending device",
    "inactive seats and rotated codes cannot request or finish stale grants",
    "a short-lived grant is single-use, exact-session retry is idempotent and expiry rejects",
    "finish requires a newly issued real Auth session for the exact business",
    "session expiry is bounded by 24 hours and the actual personal owner session",
    "refresh preserves the same actual session binding and a forged replacement session fails",
    "member and device revocation delete real Auth sessions and prevent current JWT reads",
    "removed devices stay blocked until an owner explicitly approves them again",
    "personal sign-out deletes dependent business Auth sessions and bindings",
    "ownership transfer revokes former owner access and only the current owner can bootstrap",
    "a bound seat cannot be replaced with another access code or direct session-table writes",
    "business profile reclassification and missing profile cannot escape the guard",
    "failed exchange cleanup only revokes its own fresh business session and expires its grant",
    "rate limiting persists denied attempts and never grants an inactive or guessed seat",
    "app users and anonymous callers cannot invoke any provider contract or read device secrets",
    "media service redemption checks current business owner binding even when its own Auth session survives",
    "the actual reserve/create/finish contract supports an explicit bound owner launch with a synthetic provider"
  ],
  "allPassed": true,
